reports.luxon-8688e266d051:
I'm formatting dates with negative (BCE) years, and the ISO date output comes out mangled:

```js
DateTime.fromObject({ year: -1, month: 1, day: 1, zone: "utc" }).toISODate();
// expected "-0001-01-01", got "00-1-01-01"

DateTime.fromObject({ year: -10, month: 1, day: 1, zone: "utc" }).toISODate();
// expected "-0010-01-01", got "00-10-01-01"
```

The minus sign seems to be counted as one of the digits that get zero-padded, so the year is shifted and the leading zeros end up in the wrong place. Positive years pad correctly, so this only shows up for years before 1 CE.

